{:edb/db-before-t 1643 :edb/db-after-t 1644 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534956 50 #inst "2026-10-12T22:48:32.199Z" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186194507 1078 #edb/ref 17592186194510 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186194513 1078 #edb/ref 17592186194517 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198416 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445636 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198418 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445635 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198418 1038 #edb/ref 17592186445637 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198646 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198646 1071 "![](images/df/df0ffdd8bfb94ece82926411bfddb3affc85e802807a36cb2e8ee9b9b727633c.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y = x$ and $y = 2 - x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $λ(x, y) = 3x + 2$. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y = 1$." 13194139534956 17592186045417 false] [17592186198646 1071 "![](images/df/df0ffdd8bfb94ece82926411bfddb3affc85e802807a36cb2e8ee9b9b727633c.png)\n\nA plate occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the $x$-axis and the lines $y=x$ and $y=2-x$, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is $\\lambda (x,y)=3x+2.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $y=1.$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198646 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, notice that $D$ is a type II region with representation\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,y\\le x\\le 2-y\\},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](images/d1/d1241b56d482f24cc06d51a9aaecbc623805df0a76739201e5cbe6974e2e9c6f.png)\n\nThe distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=1$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-1|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)|y-1{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}(3x+2)(y-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[{\\int }_{y}^{2-y}3x+2\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1){[\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+2x]}_{x=y}^{x=2-y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)[\\frac{3}{2}(2-y)^{2}+2(2-y)-(\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+2y)]\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}-2y+1)(1-y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1}1-3y+3{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =10{[y-\\frac{3}{2}{y}^{2}+{y}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =10(1-\\frac{3}{2}+1-\\frac{1}{4}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198647 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198647 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D = {(x, y): 3 \\le x \\le 5, 0 \\le y \\le 1}$.\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y = 2$." 13194139534956 17592186045417 false] [17592186198647 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,3\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=2.$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186198647 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=2\\cdot 1=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{3}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{3}^{5}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y-2)^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(5-3)(\\frac{1}{3}(1-2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(0-2)^{3}) \\\\  & =M(-\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{8}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1043 #edb/ref 17592186445638 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1043 #edb/ref 17592186445639 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1043 #edb/ref 17592186445640 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1043 #edb/ref 17592186445641 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1043 #edb/ref 17592186445642 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1045 "Moments of Inertia of Laminas About Other Axes" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1046 #edb/ref 17592186445640 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048585 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445616 1053 #uuid "eb4e0c90-e4bf-5334-a41e-c9dcbc6b2de0" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445617 1080 "\\frac{6M}{5}" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445617 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [1