b/ref 17592186045487 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445635 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $y$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445635 1072 #uuid "3a407e50-1493-5ac2-abfc-afeed102785c" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445635 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}k{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot [y]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(8-0)(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8k}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{x}^{2}=\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3M}{8}{x}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}({\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{5}{x}^{5}-{x}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{2}\\cdot {[y]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot (\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3})\\cdot (1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{3M}{8}\\cdot \\frac{16}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{2M}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445633 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1069 "q-163619" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1\\}.$\nFind the moment of inertia of this plate about the line $y=-2.$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1072 #uuid "5254f44e-1aee-5d92-b378-2e98dcb05199" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445636 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point on $D$ and the line $y=-2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y+2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 2=2.$ Since the plate has uniform density, the mass density function is given by\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=-2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}|y+2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{M}{2}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}({\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{-1}^{1}(y+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}\\cdot [x]_{1}^{2}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}(y+2)^{3}]}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(2-1)(\\frac{1}{3}(1+2)^{3}-\\frac{1}{3}(-1+2)^{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{2}(9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445632 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1069 "q-163664" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1071 "A rectangular plate of mass $M$ occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\nThe mass density at each point is proportional to the square of its distance from the $x$-axis. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the line $x=2.$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1072 #uuid "bff66772-3aa9-52e4-ae38-3aff93ff5b7b" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445637 1074 "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $l$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nFirst, the distance between a point and the line $x=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|x-2|.\n$$\n\nNext, the mass density can be written as $\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2},$ where $k$ is a constant of proportionality. We can find the value of $k$ by integrating the mass density function over the plate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}k{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =k({\\int }_{-3}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =k\\cdot [x]_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{3}(0-(-3))(27-1) \\\\  & =26k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=k{y}^{2}=\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $x=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}|x-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-3}^{0}{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{M}{26}{y}^{2}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}({\\int }_{-3}^{0}(x-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x)({\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot {[\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3}]}_{-3}^{0}\\cdot {[\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot (-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{125}{3})\\cdot (9-\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{26}\\cdot 39\\cdot \\frac{26}{3} \\\\  & =13M.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445638 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445641 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445638 1062 #uuid "07466f53-e252-509d-8a34-a405145acef5" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445638 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198647 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445639 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445642 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445639 1062 #uuid "75f7502b-d79d-5e16-8da0-486fac5f9f4b" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445639 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445635 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445640 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445638 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445640 1062 #uuid "af1f1335-4b99-5b58-9b75-fe6f46cf00ad" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445640 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198646 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445641 1058 #edb/ref 17592186445639 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445641 1062 #uuid "bf1ba95f-9b2b-5cae-8cac-39eec0a7a2c4" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445641 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445636 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445642 1062 #uuid "f0e756d4-4310-5dd8-bca5-e3e7d601cc8a" 13194139534956 17592186045417 true] [17592186445642 1063 #edb/ref 17592186445637 13194139534956 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"activity-eb4e0c90-e4bf-5334-a41e-c